# Files Git does not track. A pattern starting with `/` (or with a `/` in the
# middle) only matches from the repository root; one without matches at any
# depth. A trailing `/` matches directories only.
#
# Output directories are anchored to where the tools write them. A bare
# `target/`, `dist/` or `coverage/` would also ignore any source directory
# with that name, such as a module for the domain's `Target` type, and on
# Windows (case-insensitive) `Dist/` or `Coverage/` too.
#
# Cargo.lock and pnpm-lock.yaml are committed on purpose: they pin the exact
# dependency versions that were tested and reviewed.

# --- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------

# Cargo, for the workspace and for the Tauri crate.
/target/
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/target/

# Vite builds of the desktop frontend and the extension.
/apps/desktop/dist/
/extension/dist/

# Tauri: schemas generated for capability auto-completion. The rest of gen/
# (Android and iOS projects) is source and is committed.
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# WiX: the installer project builds into bin/ and obj/. Anchored to installer/
# because Cargo's src/bin/ directories are source.
/installer/**/bin/
/installer/**/obj/
*.msi
*.wixpdb

# A packed browser extension.
*.crx

# --- Dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/

# --- Coverage ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Vitest reports (in each project's own directory), cargo-llvm-cov reports
# written to the repository root (its HTML report goes to target/), and raw
# LLVM profiling data.
/coverage/
/apps/desktop/coverage/
/extension/coverage/
lcov.info
*.profraw
*.profdata

# --- Logs and crash dumps ----------------------------------------------------

*.log
*.dmp

# --- Local secrets -----------------------------------------------------------

# Environment files. Commit a `.env.example` with placeholder values instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Private keys and certificates: code signing (.pfx, .p12, and .pvk for the
# legacy Authenticode format), the key Chrome writes when it packs an
# extension (.pem), the app updater's signing key (.key).
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pvk
*.pem
*.key

# Local SQLite databases and their -wal, -shm and -journal sidecar files. A
# development database holds personal history and blocklists. A test fixture
# that really needs one must be un-ignored explicitly with `!`.
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*

# --- Editors and tools -------------------------------------------------------

# VS Code: only the recommended extensions are shared.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# JetBrains IDEs, Visual Studio (WiX projects), Vim swap files.
.idea/
.vs/
*.swp

# Claude Code: personal local settings and instructions. The shared agents in
# .claude/agents/ and CLAUDE.md are committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# --- Operating systems -------------------------------------------------------

Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
